<%# This period has already been distributed. Local: `presenter` (DistributionPresenter).

    Confirming REPLACES that split rather than adding to it, and every figure below is already
    the as-if-undistributed one — so without this line the screen would silently propose
    handing out money the user has already handed out, and a user who cannot see that their
    last split is about to be discarded cannot consent to discarding it. %>
<div class="rounded border border-status-warning bg-status-warning-light px-6 py-4">
  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-status-warning">You've already distributed this period</p>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-700">
    That split — <%= pluralize(presenter.replaced.size, "movement") %>,
    <%= number_to_currency(presenter.replaced_total) %> moved — is shown below as if it had never
    happened, because confirming replaces it rather than adding to it.
  </p>
</div>
